      "proposed_content": "The modified Mellin product law turns index addition in the moment family into contour convolution: lower-order transforms can be recombined to represent Z_{k+l}, while double inversion localizes useful frequency pairs near an antidiagonal. In the k=l=2 specialization, the paper then uses the global eighth-moment scale as a heuristic stress test on how small all local oscillatory spectral blocks could be, motivating the square-root scale of Conjecture 3.",
