    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a4b8af4237ceaf9e58f88c52aba98beddf9463d9d036198d3e7ba9fe75adcc0d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Smoothing has two source-demonstrated roles: it creates analytic localization that permits contour displacement, tail control, and frequency truncation, but it can also average away the sharp unit-window oscillation sought in Conjecture 3. Retaining phase information can remove an artificial smoothing-width restriction in a pointwise theorem without supplying the missing desmoothing step for the conjectural spectral sum.",
